["ItemText"] = {
["GameObject-620326"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Patience! A caring heart!\r\n\r\nTo beseech Kulzi, the pangolin loa of medicine, you must have both.\r\n\r\nKulzi judges not the person, the wounds, the sickness, or their reason. He heals all, no matter the season.\r\n\r\nHe is called by many names.\r\n\r\nThe Living Cure\r\n\r\nHealer of Healers\r\n\r\nReverent Doctor\r\n\r\nThe Healing Claw\r\n\r\nAll call on Kulzi to heal their wounds, their sickness, their hearts and heads.\r\n\r\nHe will use his magic or prescribe the cure.\r\n\r\nBut take heed: not all healing is within Kulzi's grasp. Make haste to his shrine if you are ailing. Lest the next loa you beseech be Jan'alai, the loa of life and death.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Kulzi",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620326,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-252385"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I am Illysanna, daughter of the resistance commander Kur'talos Ravencrest. You should know by now that my father is dead. I am not the only one who has lost someone. Our great empire, our entire world, is burning before our eyes.\r\n\r\nNothing in this war with the Burning Legion has gone according to plan. Nothing. Every battle we win is followed by two defeats. Every demon we slay is replaced by ten more.\r\n\r\nLike my father, I was once so certain of victory. So overconfident. So foolish. Most resistance fighters still are. They hold tight to their archaic ways, unwilling to accept that we cannot best our enemy through conventional means. We are fighting something alien to this world, something born of nightmare.\r\n\r\nThere is one elf who understands this: Illidan Stormrage. He knows that to defeat the demons, we must adapt. We must embrace extraordinary new tactics. If not, we will die. It is as simple as that.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Perhaps you consider Illidan an arrogant sorcerer, or even a menace to our way of life. I once did, but my opinions have changed. I am writing to explain why, and to chronicle what I have learned of Illidan. Despite his dangerous reputation, I believe he is our only chance of surviving the days ahead.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Torn Page",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252385,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-526903"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Light catches glittering script scrawled across the marble walls. Each of the countless names enchanted on the wall sports a different handwriting, from elegant lettering befitting a Magister's thesis spellbook cover to blocky script belaying a child's lack of learning. Some slanted in anger or looped in sorrow.>\r\n\r\nIn honor of those whose blood was shed to secure the survival of our people.\r\n\r\nThough the Eternal Sun may set on our darkest day.\r\n\r\nIt rises again with the coming of the dawn.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Memorial Plaque",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 526903,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-656417"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<When the sun rises, we wear our prayer charms.\r\n\r\nWhen noon arrives, we grind our offerings.\r\n\r\nWhen the sun sets, we seal it away.\r\n\r\nWhen the night falls, we rest our bones... then do it all again.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Mysterious Tablet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 656417,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-191034"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "King Greymane,\r\n\r\nThe ally you sent to aid us was most effective, and in return for your patience, I offer welcome news.\r\n\r\nWith the formation of the new Desolate Council, one of the first topics I propose is the withdrawal of Forsaken troops from the kingdom of Gilneas. In time I hope that we may come closer to agreement, and see both lands into a brighter future.\r\n\r\nWarm Regards,\r\n\r\nCalia Menethil\r\n<The Pallid Lady>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Letter to Greymane",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 191034,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["Item-145311"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Though victory was theirs, the mortal races found themselves in a world shattered by war. The Scourge and the Burning Legion had all but destroyed the civilizations of Lordaeron, and had almost finished the job in Kalimdor. There were forests to heal, grudges to bury, and homelands to settle. The war had wounded each race deeply, but they had selflessly banded together to attempt a new beginning, starting with the uneasy truce between the Alliance and Horde.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Thrall led the orcs to the continent of Kalimdor, where they founded a new homeland with the help of their tauren brethren. Naming their new land Durotar after Thrall's murdered father, the orcs settled down to rebuild their once-glorious society.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "Now that the demon curse was ended, the Horde changed from a warlike juggernaut into more of a loose coalition, dedicated to survival and prosperity rather than conquest. Aided by the noble tauren and the cunning trolls of the Darkspear tribe, Thrall and his orcs looked forward to a new era of peace in their own land.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "The remaining Alliance forces under Jaina Proudmoore settled in southern Kalimdor. Off the eastern coast of Dustwallow Marsh, they built the rugged port city of Theramore. There, the humans and their dwarven allies worked to survive in a land that would always be hostile to them. Though the defenders of Durotar and Theramore kept the tentative truce with one another, the fragile colonial serenity was not meant to last.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "The peace between the orcs and humans was shattered by the arrival of a massive Alliance fleet in Kalimdor. The mighty fleet, under the command of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore (Jaina's father), had left Lordaeron before Arthas had destroyed the kingdom. Having sailed for many grueling months, Admiral Proudmoore was searching for any Alliance survivors he could find.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "Proudmoore's armada posed a serious threat to the stability of the region. As a renowned hero of the Second War, Jaina's father was a staunch enemy of the Horde, and he was determined to destroy Durotar before the orcs could gain a foothold in the land.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "The Grand Admiral forced Jaina to make a terrible decision: support him in battle against the orcs and betray her newfound allies, or fight her own father to maintain the fragile peace that the Alliance and the Horde had finally attained. After much soul-searching, Jaina chose the latter and helped Thrall defeat her crazed father. ",
},
{
["Page"] = 8,
["Text"] = "Unfortunately Admiral Proudmoore died in battle before Jaina could reconcile with him or prove that orcs were no longer bloodthirsty monsters. For her loyalty, the orcs allowed Jaina's forces to return home safely to Theramore.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Old Hatreds - The Colonization of Kalimdor",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 145311,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["Item-203475"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Gyre, \r\n\r\nThere is an urgent mission that requires a seasoned champion of Stormwind such as yourself. \r\n\r\nQuickly, meet me behind Stormwind Keep, and tell no one!\r\n\r\n<The paper is not signed, only branded with with an insignia of SI:7.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Urgent Stormwind Summons",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 203475,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-579123"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "They believe its silent vigil kept the horrors of the rift at bay. But the flame dimmed and the horrors escaped. Eventually, the flame was moved to preserve it.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Words of Obayo--Part 1: The Flame",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579123,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-525293"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Gather as much lightwood as you are able. The elves will know we are here soon enough. We must arm ourselves before they do. See it done!\r\n\r\n--Zul'jan",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Amani Missive",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 525293,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-669320"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I HAVE SEEN SUCH HORRORS IN LIFE\r\nI COMMIT MYSELF TO AN EVERLASTING DEATH\r\nTO SAVE MY CHILDREN AND THEIR CHILDREN\r\nFROM THE EVIL THAT DEFEATED DARKNESS\r\n\r\nTHE SNAKES MUST REMAIN SEALED AWAY\r\nTHE WEAPON IS AS DEADLY AS THE VOID\r\nOUR SHAME MUST REMAINED BURIED\r\nI PROUDLY PAY THE ETERNAL PRICE",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "LET MY SPIRIT GUARD THESE HALLS\r\nLET MY SHADE BAR THE WAY\r\nLET NO AMANI OR TRESSPASSING THIEF\r\nCROSS THE THRESHOLD\r\n\r\n- ZAZ'KE THE GUARDIAN",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Profaned Plaque",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 669320,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613887"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<A handwritten sheet of music intended for the lyre, only partially filled in. The thin paper is brittle with age.>\r\n\r\n\r\n\"Dawn's Caress\"\r\n\r\nDedicated to His Grace, Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider\r\n\r\n\r\nComposer - Lirath Windrunner",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Unfinished Sheet Music",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613887,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-252302"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Good news, everyone! No one will ever find my masterpiece!\r\n\r\nStitchwork is nearly complete. Just a few more pieces and some elbow grease, perhaps some ooze and/or gas...\r\n\r\nSuch imbeciles! They never think to look for trap doors in my lab. Well, there was that one adventurer, but now she's part of Stitchwork.\r\n\r\nNow, where did I leave my... Oh, delightful! Why am I still writing this down?",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Professor Putricide's Lost Journal",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252302,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-669312"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<There are multiple swaths of fabric that look like torn pieces of clothing, written with charcoal, sealed in the bottle with a cork stopper.>\r\n\r\nHelp! Our ship, Sethralis's Scale, has run aground.  We are on an island east of Zul'Aman. Send help and you can have the cargo we saved.\r\n\r\n- Captain Lenta",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "<The next scrap of cloth is from a fine jacket.>\r\n\r\nThe bottle came back. Again. I've thrown it out to see on the tide. This makes no sense. If you find this, tell a tortollan sailor. They will know who I am. We still have plenty of cargo to reward you if you come and rescue us.\r\n\r\n- Captain Lenta",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "<This scrap seems to be leather from a backpack.>\r\n\r\nThis bottle won't stop returning. This island is haunted and infested with snakes. We would still like to be rescued, but I understand if you stay far away from here. All we have found are wrecks of Zandalari ships. I should never have purchased a Zandalari ship. Whatever has cursed this island does not like the Zandalari. Can't it see I'm a tortollan? I hope this bottle floats away this time.\r\n \r\n- Captain Lenta",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "<The final scrap was written on a sun-bleached hat.>\r\n\r\nCaptain Lenta was bitten by a snake. Don't come here. This island is a cage.\r\n- Swabby Wuck",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Message in a Bottle",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 669312,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579240"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Our elders and our traditions say that it is our purpose to keep the land. The outside world has its own ways, and they are not our concern. Only Harandar.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "So we wait patiently for Aln'hara's return. We stare up at her Cradle, hoping to one day see it filled.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Seeker's Trail--Part 2: Seeking Peace",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579240,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-507966"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Much of this text has been worn away over the years, or made illegible with bloodstains. A bookmarked passage stands out to you.>\r\n\r\nMy Blessed Lord has gifted me with renewed life, and a new citadel from which I have been tasked the honor of overseeing a branch of his army. I, who attempted to betray him... have been rewarded. \r\n\r\nPerhaps I should have focused my studies on the curiosities of necromancy. After all, what use is the Sunwell's power if one has passed beyond the realm of the living? \r\n\r\nI am eternal, now. And I have Arthas to thank for it.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Profane Research",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 507966,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-572447"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "One of a thousand broken spears littering the Hellfire Ramparts. Whether it belonged to a Horde or Alliance soldier is unclear--time cares little for such distinctions.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Scarred Spear",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 572447,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-140263"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "THE EMERALD ASCENSION\r\n\r\nFear not the time when great Sargeras's shadow eclipses the sun. \r\n\r\nThat is the moment of our ascension. \r\n\r\nDeath will follow, but it is only a doorway. \r\n\r\nStep through, and you will shed your frail skin and take on a form kissed by emerald fire.\r\n\r\nDig the ash from your eyes, and you will find a higher purpose at Sargeras's side.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Worn Pamphlet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 140263,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-613850"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "...and while they may be mighty and regal, it is important to remember that hawkstriders are, above all else, highly nervous creatures. They must be allowed at least one hour of uninterrupted preening time per day in order to relieve stress. \r\n\r\nIt is recommended to separate hawkstriders during preening time. Do not attempt to help your hawkstrider preen, and do not permit your hawkstrider to preen you. Both can be considered displays of...\r\n\r\n<The book continues like this for several hundred pages.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Hawkstrider Husbandry: Unabridged Edition",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613850,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-669316"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Before you are glyphs on a slab of black obsidian that does not reflect the sun. The tablet feels ancient. Though it was submerged in the venom, the edges are still razor sharp and show no sign of weathering. Grime slides off the tablet, leaving it pristine. It casts a shadow darker than should be possible at this time of day.>\r\n\r\n<The text is written in simple angular letters. Yet while reading it, each word seems to burn itself into your eyes, leaving an afterimage of the dark letters when you close your aching eyes. You hear faint whispers, and a great feeling of hopelessness overcomes you until you release the tablet.>",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "<The shadow whispers to you. Yours is a mind that can comprehend it.>\r\n\r\nThe darkness below echoes above.\r\nThe Void persists. The Void sees all possibilities. The Void returns.\r\nGive yourself to the darkness. Give yourself to the fear.\r\nThe writhing and squirming of the endless host calls to you.\r\nTurn against the Light. Turn against Order. The Void consumes all.\r\nWhen the Void rises again, only its followers will survive.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Oily Black Stone",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 669316,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579233"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "My people came from a violent land with the hope to rise above what we were and find more. But the land had other plans.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "We faced violence at every turn, but there was one enemy that persisted. They hunted us with malice.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "The constant fight drove my people back to our old ways as hunters, and killers.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Laments of Wey'nan--Part 1: Finding Hope",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579233,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-21004"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Here lies Grommash Hellscream, Chieftain of the Warsong Clan\r\n\r\nIn many ways, the curse of our people began and ended with Grom.\r\nHis name meant 'giant's heart' in our ancient tongue. He earned that \r\nname a hundred-fold as he stood alone before the demon Mannoroth \r\n- and won our freedom with his blood. \r\n\r\nLok'Tar ogar, big brother. May the Warsong never fade. \r\n\r\n-Thrall, Warchief of the Horde \r\n",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Monument to Grom Hellscream",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 21004,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-265820"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Why must we remain hidden in our caves, when the whole world could be blessed by our prowess and knowledge? We protect her roots while they burn her lands? They need us. We do her a disservice by remaining here!\r\n\r\nThe simpletons have given us all the power I need. With the Lightbloom returned to their lands, they can be pruned to a manageable size. Why should these surface dwellers rule themselves? I am the wise one. I am the strong one. I am Aln'hara's chosen.\r\n\r\nThe others will see. They will understand!\r\n\r\nIn due time...",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ruia's Musings, Part 3",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 265820,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-180516"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "You have discovered the location of the shrine!  Upon further examination, you sense a stronger pulse of the strange power that has gripped the Isle.  You feel a bit uncomfortable standing by the shrine... and perhaps a little disturbed.\r\n\r\nThe bronze placard along the side of the shrine reads:\r\n\r\n\"Here stands the Shrine of Dath'Remar, a fitting tribute to a noble elf.  Let all who gaze on this monument remember his sacrifices for our people and his dedication to the cause of our continued survival.  All who prosper in Quel'Thalas do so thanks to him.\"",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Shrine of Dath'Remar",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 180516,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579203"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The Hara'ti believe this is where Aln'hara once rested, and where one day she will return. We call this the Cradle.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "The haranir believe it is her song that calls to the roots and guides them here. Once the roots reach the Cradle, and join the Rootways, it strengthens the land. Not every great tree's roots have reached the Cradle, such is the wisdom of Aln'hara. In her absence, the roots must be tended and protected. This is why she called the haranir to this land.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Awe'ohna's Path--Part 3: The Cradle",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579203,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579183"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "If you listen to the roots, they will tell you of most threats. But what of threats they do not recognize? If we prune roots they see as healthy, will we be forgiven? Will the roots trust us again?",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ways of the Roots--Part 3: Pruning",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579183,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-693666"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The unnatural blue flame emanating from this torch is untouched by the breeze blowing through the chamber.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Hexed Flame",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 693666,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-619613"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The dark loa whispered to me of a great lock and key, together beneath the earth.\r\n\r\nThe dark loa whispered to me of a great devastation.\r\n\r\nWhat have we buried that can rise again?\r\n\r\nWhat fool would forget where the end of the world begins?",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Pilfered Amani Tablet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 619613,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-669314"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This journal has faded and the ink has run from being submerged in water.>\r\n\r\nFrom the logbook of boson Khan'yee.\r\n\r\nWe are sailing in circles.  \r\n\r\nThe storm drove toward the shore, within sight of elven lands. Rather than risk confrontation, the captain took us close to Zul'Aman. We knew the risks, not of the forest, but of the island. The island no one comes back from.\r\n\r\nThe winds were the first to betray us. They pushed us toward the mist, changing as we tried to tack away from certain doom. The air felt wrong. It was foul smelling and acrid--it would sting the eyes and fester wounds.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "The currents and tides changed next. Pulling us toward the rocks. Pulling us toward that Island. With wind and waves working together to sink the ship, the crew panicked. They fought each other more than the forces that intended to dash us against the rocks.\r\n\r\nThe hull has been holed, but still we are dragged in. The mists surround us. I can see something on the shore writhing in the sand. We will have to leave the wreckage of our once fine ship. Hopefully the rumors of this place prove false.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "<There are no other entries.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Zandalari Logbook",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 669314,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-651055"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "In honor of Zek'ara the Unseen, who walked ahead of every war party and returned with truths the jungle did not wish to give. She mapped the paths others could not follow.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Zek'ara de Unseen",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 651055,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-693668"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The invaders went out of their way to desecrate this tablet honoring a hero of the Amani.\r\n\r\nWhoever it was must harbor great spite for the native trolls.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Broken Tablet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 693668,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-265818"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Har'alnor remains calm. Must keep an eye on the rutaani encampment: they seem more agitated today. Perhaps an outlier, but something to watch.\r\n\r\nPossibly related: the area around the roots have been infused with a new light. Strange. Unwelcome.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "It does not seem to be causing a problem as of yet, but I am suspicious of anything that I cannot verify with my own experiences. Where did this strange light come from? What is it doing? Who sent this?\r\n\r\nIt is my sacred duty as a Rootwarden to solve this problem. There are more frivolous among us who would rest on their laurels.\r\n\r\nAln'hara as my witness, the other elders will understand my wisdom.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ruia's Musings, Part 1",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 265818,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-618569"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Theris, \r\n\r\nI knew you wouldn't understand. Even if I couched my reasoning in platitudes about protecting the family, protecting Silvermoon, you always see right through me, don't you? \r\n\r\nThen, fine. You win. You're right. \r\n\r\nMany ren'dorei chose this path out of a desire to understand that which we must defeat: The Void. They have made a noble sacrifice in order to save their people, even as they are shunned for it. \r\n\r\nBut not me. No, I am honest with myself. I did this for me.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tattered Page",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618569,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-58937"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Ogerin'naz makogg kil Tov'nokaz kagg kaz tov'osh ko g lok'tar osh'kazil il makogg Lok'mogul.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Blackrock Invasion Plans",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 58937,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-668597"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "To those I failed: I will sing your valor. Before you lies eternity, may glory be your everlasting companion.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Funerary Inscription",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 668597,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-654586"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This tablet has been worn by the elements. Most of the words are illegible.>\r\n\r\n\r\nIn     jungle of bright green\r\n      fought and      and then    \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n                   her fangs",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Worn Tablet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 654586,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-618558"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This ren'dorei telescope seems at first like it's pointed in the direction of the distant Voidspire. When you put your eye to the lens, the telescope focuses in on a distant nest of flying beasts slightly to its left.\r\n\r\nThe armature of the stand is dotted in a fine mist of crimson blood and a shred of silver cloth in ren'dorei style. Claw marks mar the ground between your feet. They stretch all the way to the edge of the cliff and then disappear, pointed in the same direction as that nest.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Abandoned Telescope",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618558,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-555786"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "By order of Grand Magister Rommath, and ratified by Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron, the sin'dorei hereby bestow ownership of the Umbral Atrium to Magister Umbric and his ren'dorei in good standing with Silvermoon.\r\n\r\nLet none forget the sacrifice and heroism of the ren'dorei in Silvermoon's darkest hour.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Deed to the Umbral Atrium",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 555786,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-252386"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I first met Illidan in the early stages of the war, back when I considered the Burning Legion a passing threat. The night elf resistance was headquartered at my family's ancestral home, the great fortress of Black Rook Hold. Those days were glorious to behold. Thousands of elves gathered at the stronghold from the far ends of the empire, all sworn to defend our lands against the demons.\r\n\r\nAs the daughter of Commander Ravencrest, I enjoyed a position of power and privilege. I attended council meetings with sorcerers from the Moon Guard, priestesses from the Sisterhood of Elune, and other influential figures. I also crossed paths with lesser-known resistance members-elves like Illidan.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Illidan came to Black Rook Hold with his brother, the druid Malfurion Stormrage, and the priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. I met the trio only briefly, and they did not leave any lasting impressions on me. Illidan in particular seemed like just one more sorcerer among the hundreds who had joined the resistance.\r\n\r\nYet soon, everyone would know his name. And some, like me, would come to distrust him.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Worn-Edged Page",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252386,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-645553"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The text has mainly been worn away with time but perhaps it says...Jin'ta?>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Nameless Grave",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 645553,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-651052"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "In honor of Vol'seya, Storm-Touched of Akil'zon, whose eyes saw beyond the horizon and whose words carried the weight of distant thunder. She gave her sight that others might see.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Vol'seya de Storm-Touched",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 651052,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-265819"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Disgusting! Irresponsible! Reprehensible!\r\n\r\nIt would be the surface dwellers who would taint the sanctity of Harandar with their curses.\r\n\r\nTheir light spreads across the land like an infection blooming across our pristine fields, inciting the afflicted rutaani to madness. It must be stopped before it goes any further... and before the other elders hear that it happened on my watch.\r\n\r\nNo matter. A haranir will succeed where others have failed. This is a certainty.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ruia's Musings, Part 2",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 265819,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["Item-58936"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Ogar moguna nogu ha gul'rok ha raznos. Ogg regas gesh'zugas throm'ka gi mog moth'aga.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Blackrock Orc Missive",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 58936,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-553839"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Devastation\r\n\r\nWarriors of the sin'dorei are normally known for spear, bow, and sword, but Thaladred the Darkener preferred an axe above all. First used during the Troll Wars, Devastation struck its enemies with such brutality that their swift regeneration, magic, and even calls to their loa would fail them.\r\n\r\nAlthough its origins lay in defense of Quel'Thalas, Thaladred wielded the weapon in service of the traitor Prince Kael'thas in later years. In doing so, he betrayed his people and forever stained the weapon's legacy. Until a day when one is found with the unique temperament to wield it, Devasation bathes in the light of the Sunwell, in the hopes of removing the Darkener's shadow.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Devastation",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 553839,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-625401"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "What wretch am I to be burdened by this knowledge.\r\n\r\nWhat curiosity that brings the Amani to uncover---\r\n\r\nWhat should remain lost---\r\n\r\nWhat destroys---",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Damaged Amani Tablet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 625401,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-245381"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<HTML><BODY>\r\n<BR/><BR/>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">Uther the Lightbringer</H1>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Common\\spacer\" align=\"center\" width=\"1\" height=\"27\"/>\r\n<P>\r\nFirst paladin, father of the original Order of the Silver Hand, guiding light for all. May we honor his legacy in all that we do.\r\n</P>\r\n</BODY></HTML>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Uther the Lightbringer",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 245381,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-369228"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "ARCHIVIST ROH-LUDA, RELIC RESTORER\r\n\r\nThe afterlives of the Shadowlands give rise to many curious, fantastic, and unstable relics. It is our Purpose to catalog, curate, study, and safeguard them.\r\n\r\nBy our ministrations, we will better understand the nature of each afterlife, we will comprehend how disparate souls fit in the fabric of existence, and perhaps most importantly, we will keep potentially dangerous relics out of the hands of those who would misuse them.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Archivist Roh-Luda's Teachings",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 369228,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-669317"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Carved in the stone with a quick and casual style.>\r\n\r\nRULES FOR THE FORUM \r\n\r\nWHEN MASON'S CHISEL BENDS\r\nWHEN LABORER'S BACK BREAKS\r\nWHEN WARRIOR'S SPEAR BLUNTS\r\nGATHER THE FRUSTRATED\r\nHEAD TO THE FORUM \r\n\r\nIF A TROLL SPEAKS ILL\r\nINTERRUPT THEIR SPEECH\r\nNAME THEM FOOL\r\nASK WHO BAKED THEIR BREAD\r\nASK WHO GAVE THEM BOOTS \r\n\r\nIF WORKERS CLASH AND FIGHT\r\nIF LABORERS SHOUT AND QUARREL\r\nIF WARRIORS GRUMBLE OVER ORDERS\r\nQUOTE THEM CROOKED\r\nLET ALL REMEMBER YOUR WORDS INSTEAD",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "LET NO QUARREL DIE\r\nLET NO TROLL FIND ACCORD\r\nLET NO AMANI REFLECT\r\nAS LONG AS ONE HAS BREATH TO BELLOW\r\n\r\nTHUS IS BLOOD KEPT FROM TEMPLE STONE\r\nSPILL IT IN THE FORUM\r\nFIGHT IN THIS EMPTY SPACE\r\nGAIN NOTHING BUT THE SATISFACTION\r\nTHAT SOMEONE WAS WRONG",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Forum Rules",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 669317,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-693662"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The energies that emanate from this ritual mask differ from the latent energies of the crypt.\r\n\r\nThe magic feels very familiar.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Hex Mask",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 693662,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-556449"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "We the undersigned agree to the following compact. That in times of great need and world ending threats, past grievances and vengeance can be set aside to allow the greatest minds of might and magic to come together and find solutions to craft war against such threats.\r\n\r\nLet all who follow this compact use this magic and wisdom for the betterment and defense of Azeroth and her citizens.\r\n\r\nIn the face of evil that threatens Azeroth herself, let those practitioners of magic once again work together for a better future.\r\n\r\nIn memory of Theramore, Dalaran, and the Sunwell.\r\n\r\nQuel'falan danas! \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSigned,\r\n\r\nVereesa Windrunner                                  Aethas Sunreaver\r\n\r\n\r\nWitnessed by Font.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "The Silversun Compact",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 556449,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-292838"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The Approach of the Worthy\r\n\r\nYou will be judged. You will be measured. The Serpent shall decide your fate.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Placard",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 292838,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579242"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Both are necessary for Harandar to thrive, so we must protect both. But they are fundamentally different and cannot stand the other's presence. I fear only Aln'hara's return will bring them real peace.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tending the Lands--Part 1: The Conflict",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579242,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-653374"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This piece of paper was once crumpled up in frustration.>\r\n\r\nOraka-zul Ulantu,\r\n\r\nI received your message asking to be assigned a different shaman bodyguard.\r\n\r\nI deny your request. Naj'kula is also a talented fire shaman, one of the most talented I have ever seen. That is why I asked her to join you, my most talented scout.\r\n\r\nThe other issues I would chalk up to communication. Something I know you're not good at.\r\n\r\nGive it some time, Ulantu. You may come to respect her gifts as I have come to respect hers and yours.\r\n\r\nKul'amara",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "A Message from Kul'amara",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 653374,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579241"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Some feel the call, and hunt for the missing goddess. We have scoured every inch of Harandar, as our traditions allow.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Some seek the goddess far beyond Harandar. The elders do not approve, but when they hear the call, all they can do is seek. Though it is almost unheard of in the past centuries, legends claim that in ancient time enough haranir left that they could have formed new tribes. We are, after all, hunters. But none have found her, and where could you hide a goddess?",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Seeker's Trail--Part 3: Unending Mission",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579241,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-270268"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "These words of the Hexlord are meant for Zul'jan, grandson of Zul'jin.\r\n\r\nEmpower the Fang and you will gain the ability to control the Children of Ula'tek. Like any weapon, they must be mastered. Once you are ready, we will show the Amani, and they will know you have returned your people to greatness.\r\n\r\nThey will understand. Even your sister.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Crumpled Note",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 270268,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-618571"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The Shadowgraft hums. It calls to you with the promise of power.\r\n\r\nYou reach a hand out before you can stop yourself. As your skin touches the cold metal, you feel a rush of power.\r\n\r\nThe thrill of battle. The soaring heartbeat of a duel. The off-beat note of a parry.\r\n\r\nThe brutal satisfaction of sinking your blade into your enemy's flesh, that feeling both disgusting and triumphant.\r\n\r\nYour fingers tingle. Your vision is red. You have already grabbed your weapon, turning to fight the next enemy.\r\n\r\nAs you step away from the Shadowgraft, your vision returns to normal. Your breath returns and your heartbeat slows.\r\n\r\nYou know deep in your bones that this metal will make you braver and stronger.\r\n\r\nYou also know that if you are bound by it, you will never be yourself again.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Shadowgraft Harness",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618571,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620323"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Heart! Inner Fire!\r\n\r\nThose who follow Jan'alai have both.\r\n\r\nJan'alai--the dragonhawk that from ash lights the dawn, at birth and at death we hear their song.\r\n\r\nThey are called by many names.\r\n\r\nThe Everlasting Fire\r\n\r\nThe Twisting Flame\r\n\r\nThe Crucible\r\n\r\nThe Searing Truth\r\n\r\nThe Mistress and Master of Magic\r\n\r\nThe Shadowpine call upon Jan'alai to stoke their inner fire, fan the flames of their magic, fuel their desires. Life and death are under their wings, as are the songs her shamans sing. Jan'alai brings us life, ushers us through death and night, tracing the sun on its journey through time. The hatchling, the sage--they are one in the cycle of the dragonhawk loa, Jan'alai, patron of life, death, renewal, magic, and the FIRE in all Amani hearts!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Jan'alai",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620323,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579234"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "All of the rutaani have been hostile, but these Zaratti push us to our limits. The others fear us, but because of their leader, these rutaani hate us and hunt us at every turn.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Zarat, the leader of this grove of rutaani, sees us as trespassers and interlopers. If these creatures have hearts, the leader knows how to turn them against us. Can we find peace with them? Should we?",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "We were called here for a greater purpose. We could hunt and fight on Hyjal. We must find that purpose here, no matter the cost. These Zaratti cannot stand in our way.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Laments of Wey'nan--Part 2:  Hunting Purpose",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579234,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-653579"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I, Esa'ne, have done the impossible! I sailed the Strait of Hexx'alor and escaped Zul'jin's tyranny. The brute planned to have my tongue cut and my forehead branded. Damn him, damn the Horde that abandoned us, and damn those elves most of all. I'd rather die a free Amani than live chasing the wars of alien monsters.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "I have survived one summer so far. Atal'Utek is as they said. Shrouded in mists almost always. I have learned to hone my other senses. I hear voices in the night, and I see shapes moving in the dark. I avoid the ruins where their green lights flicker. But the land here is fertile and the beasts fat. My spear finds their bellies easily, and I eat well.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "In my heart, revenge burns. My boat was shattered on the rocks. But someday, I will return to Zul'Aman. \r\n\r\nIf I fail, let those who find my bones know Zul'jin is the bastard son of a harpy and no true Amani.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Amani Exile's Words",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 653579,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-669318"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<A faded and waterlogged journal written in ancient Zandalari script.>\r\n\r\nThere are only snakes to eat on this accursed island. What little edible plants we find will not sate our hunger. We thought the Amani conquered these lands. But we must hunt. We must eat. And there are only snakes.\r\n\r\nIf you find this journal, you must be trapped here as well. You might be Zandalari, or from our ships. Let me help you, my brothers and sisters. Let me teach you how to survive a day longer than the crew of the Golden Sunrise.\r\n\r\nRule 1: The head will kill you, even in death.\r\n\r\nIf you survive the hunt and kill the snake, beware the head. It will bite. Even when dead. Even when removed. It will lunge at you and pierce your flesh. It will inject you with its venom. Even removed from the body, it will bite. Bury it before you cook the body.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Rule 2: Beware the sacs.\r\n\r\nCut off not just the head--cut off the neck. Where is the neck on a snake? Choose to risk hunger rather than risk eating a venom sac. Eat from the tail up until you learn where the lowest sac is on the body. You will discover where this line is when your friend gives in to their hunger and dies.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "Rule 3: Burn your meat.\r\n\r\nCooking your meal is good. Burning your meal is better. Fire will purge what venom has seeped into the flesh. Be patient. Let the snake char. It won't taste good, but you will survive the meal.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "Rule 4: The venom will get you.\r\n\r\nYou will not survive. But hungry castaways die faster. That may be for the best. Reflect on how you want to go. The venom is not peaceful, but it is quick.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Survival Journals",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 669318,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-651050"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "In honor of Kaz'jin the Unyielding, who held the bridge at Shadra'kor alone until his brothers could cross. The river remembers his blood.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Kaz'jin the Unyielding",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 651050,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-618542"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This regal domanaar armor sits in a heavy silence. Despite its expert make, an aura of malice warps the breastplate's perfection. It is displayed alongside the following inscription.>\r\n\r\nVaras, whose greatest delight was martial prowess, raised Obscurion Citadel from nothing. He donned the impenetrable Lorica Umbra in battle. It turned away every blade or spell that sought to harm its wearer.\r\n\r\nWhen the Devouring Host demanded he surrender, Varas refused. With his armor, he could not be defeated.\r\n\r\nBut then, Xal'atath came to Varas alone. She whispered words into his ear that are known only between them. After a pause, Varas removed the Lorica Umbra. Then, at Xal'atath's command, he was killed.\r\n\r\nShe is the Void. Think to stand above her, this fate too shall be yours.\r\n\r\n-Lord Terminas\r\n\r\n<The Lorica Umbra has no chance of fitting you.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Void Armor",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618542,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-241470"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<HTML><BODY>\r\n<BR/><BR/>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">General Lena Stormpike</H1>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Common\\spacer\" align=\"center\" width=\"1\" height=\"27\"/>\r\n<P>\r\nA stalwart combatant and defender of justice, fallen defending her home from the foul demons of the Burning Legion. Azeroth is darker for her passing.\r\n</P>\r\n</BODY></HTML>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "General Lena Stormpike",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 241470,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-180088"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "To my love,\r\n\r\nI confess that I remember. By some miracle, this echo of our past found me. I saved it, and with it, saved all that we were.\r\n\r\nPerhaps it was my undoing. I scorned the Archon's trust and so fell prey to this nightmare.\r\n\r\nBut the flicker of you comforts me in my final moments. Fate is blind to this horizon, but may we be as one anew.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Handwritten Note",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 180088,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-693664"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The skull is studded with jewels and covered in magical sigils.\r\n\r\nIt looks to be a necromancer's ritual focus.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ornate Skull",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 693664,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-191733"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Malygos, my Aspect...\r\n\r\nThe dracthyr remain securely in stasis, and my long vigil watching over them continues. While I am reluctant to trouble you, I fear I must report that the integrity of this creche has been compromised.\r\n\r\nAn insectoid infestation has breached these halls. In my own arrogance, I at first believed this incursion would prove little more than an annoyance of unwanted pests.\r\n\r\nBut now the contamination spreads out of control, and I find myself short of breath as I am overwhelmed by the toxins produced by this invasive species.\r\n\r\nI refuse to abandon the post you assigned to me, but I must request additional aid. It seems my arcane skills are insufficient to counteract this malady.\r\n\r\nYour loyal servant,\r\n\r\nAndesigos",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Report: Infestation",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 191733,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-651053"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "In honor of Maz'dul the Ember-Keeper, tender of the sacred flame that burned without fuel for two generations. When he died, the flame died with him.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Maz'dul de Embah-Keepah",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 651053,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-553910"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Netherstrand Longbow\r\n\r\nThere are some who claim the Netherstrand Longbow was first carried by the Highborne in the War of the Ancients. Others say that it was not forged until Kael'thas journeyed to Outland and saw the expanse of the Twisting Nether with his own eyes.\r\n\r\nWhat is known is that strands of magic drawn from the Twisting Nether itself make the Netherstrand one of the deadliest bows ever used. The longbow was recovered from Outland after the forces of Kael'thas used it against the draenei. Perhaps its damaged legacy can be purified in the light of the Sunwell.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Netherstrand Longbow",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 553910,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579239"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Aln'hara is no longer in Harandar, but her song remains. It is ingrained through every inch of the land and every beast within it.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "The haranir were called to this land to keep it safe until she returns, and to renew the song. So we tend this land and wait.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Seeker's Trail--Part 1: Call of Aln'hara",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579239,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579182"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Many of the roots, and the Cradle, were here long before the haranir. Many came later. Nordrassil, Shaladrassil, Teldrassil, and others were planted over countless ages by those on the surface, but the roots reached out to Harandar.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "The roots speak their names in the languages of the surface folk who planted them. If the roots reach Harandar, we know Aln'hara blesses them and we welcome them to the great knot of Harandar.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "They are tended and protected, but we cannot protect them from the dangers above. The people of that world do not always protect the trees they have planted. We heal what we can. The branches may burn, but the roots will thrive.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ways of the Roots--Part 2: Growing",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579182,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-238500"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The rules of nature reign supreme upon this world. Every species we've stumbled upon seems designed to fight and kill. Those that aren't purely carnivores feast instead on flows of Void energy. Perhaps we ren'dorei aren't so unlike them.\r\n\r\nThis is no homeworld of Void from what we can tell. It seems instead a planet, like any other, that exists at the nexus of Void energies throughout the cosmos. I am reminded of Outland. I advise similar survival tactics to those used by our kin who called themselves Sunfury before embracing the Void. We might ask Leona Darkstrider what she learned from Adarus Duskblaze.\r\n\r\nExploring the wastes remains a high priority. Natural resources born of this world are sure to be potent in our fight against Xal'atath.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Maella's Report",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 238500,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-579244"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Although the fungarians often fear us, they will speak to us. This does not make it easier to learn from them. They answer with little thought and always have questions of their own. So many questions.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tending the Lands--Part 3: The Cycle",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579244,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579235"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Claws, fangs, instinct: they are a part of who we are, and we must not give them up. But to grow, we must learn from what we did here: fight for more than survival, learn to control what we are, and do not let it control us. Otherwise we will destroy this land, or any we live in.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Laments of Wey'nan--Part 3: There Must Be More",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579235,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-668591"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Here fell my mother and father. Together, they were the thunder and the lightning. Now the skies are clear, and they rest.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Funerary Inscription",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 668591,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-290700"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Blessings upon those who honor their ancestors. Each gift is smiled upon by the kings and queens of old. May they grant you their favor, in this life or the next.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Worn Prayer Book",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 290700,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-668599"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "To my sister, always swift of foot and sure of strength: Soundless are your footfalls now. I carry your spear, but it hangs heavy in my hand.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Funerary Inscription",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 668599,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-651054"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "In honor of Jin Drak'aja, whose word was law across seven villages and whose silence was more feared than his rage. He carried his authority on his brow.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Jin Drak'aja",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 651054,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579180"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Serve the roots, and they will serve you.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ways of the Roots--Part 1: Serving",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579180,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-57756"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The letter is missing entries as the ink has washed away in many places.>\r\n\r\n... every form of ... has been based ... on the antagonism of oppressing and oppressed ...\r\n\r\n... nothing to lose, but your chains ...\r\n\r\n... the past cannot be forgotten ...\r\n\r\n... cannot be forgiven ...\r\n\r\n... will RISE AGAIN!\r\n\r\n\r\n",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Murloc Clue",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 57756,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-668601"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "To the stranger who passes by: Know that I dine with the ancestors now. I am free from the dust of this world.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Funerary Inscription",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 668601,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-466230"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG ONE\r\n\r\nDornogal. It feels like I know this place, but I'm experiencing it for the first time. I don't quite understand it. \r\n\r\nI've talked to many of my kin, and they've explained as much as they could, but it hasn't helped at all. \r\n\r\nThis is my home, but it doesn't feel that way. \r\n\r\nI wonder if it ever will.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TWO\r\n\r\nAs the days go by, attitudes seem to be changing. My kin can be rigid and stubborn, but there's a warmth to them.\r\n\r\nI've learned about what led to my day of awakening. Tribulations that lasted millennia.  \r\n\r\nI've awoken during a shifting age. I wonder what this means for me. Where is my place?",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG THREE\r\n\r\nSpeaker Brinthe insists I come up with a name for myself. I've toyed with different names. \r\n\r\nAurora? It doesn't quite fit, but it's what I saw before I woke.  I will never forget that beautiful light, the warmth of that voice.  \r\n\r\nMaybe something vibrant like Coral?\r\n\r\nNo, that doesn't quite fit either. I'll keep thinking.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG SIX\r\n\r\nI feel less hesitant now. Adjusting to our society and all the rules has proven difficult. \r\n\r\nAs much as I love my kin, I still can't quite understand their adherence to tradition. They say it's what you're supposed to do. \r\n\r\nWhy? \r\n\r\nWhen I asked Brinthe, she had a different answer. At one point we served the Titans. \r\n\r\nBut now? \r\n\r\nNow we choose to serve one another. This has inspired me.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG NINE \r\n\r\nMy name is Dawn. \r\n\r\nI had to write this down. It came to me after watching the sun rise over Dornogal.\r\n\r\nDawn, the start of a new day, of a new age. The end of darkness, the beginning of something more. \r\n\r\nThis I feel represents who I wish to be.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TEN\r\n\r\nI've been helping the Foreman quite a bit. He has been teaching about the rigid processes that my kin used to experience. \r\n\r\nThe machines don't seem to do well with we Awakened. \r\n\r\nAnd the Foreman's language at times can be harsh. I know he doesn't mean it in that way. \r\n\r\nThank the cogs that Caretakers exist. They seem to be a bit more prepared. \r\n\r\nIt takes time to change your ways--but I hope the Foreman adjusts sooner rather than later.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TWELVE\r\n\r\nNext week I start implementing my improvements to the Awakening Protocol.\r\n\r\nI hope that they go well. Our awakening shouldn't be frightening. It should feel the same as the song's warm embrace. \r\n\r\nNo matter what happens, I do know this is a step into a new age. \r\n\r\nOne day earthen will travel beyond the shores of Khaz Algar. But for now, the first step.  \r\n\r\nOur society is changing. But there's no reason it must all be at once.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Navigations of the Soul",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 466230,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579238"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I have ignored the risks. When I was in the painting of a battle, some dark creature lashed out. I am still fevered from its venom.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "These are no mere visions, and they're more than memories. Ribs are broken, and the venom nearly reached my heart. But the rewards seem worth the price.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "I must share my secrets, and train the next generation to be wiser than I was. Create, learn, and share--but temper and be aware. Each image can bring ruin. Each memory can bring death. And the Alndust is too precious to waste. Only a few will carry this honor, to let others live our past.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Echoes of Our Past--Part 3: Dangerous Memories",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579238,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-175736"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "In the ancient times, after the Titans departed Azeroth, their children, known as the earthen, continued to shape and guard the deep recesses of the world. The earthen were largely unconcerned with the affairs of the surface-dwelling races and longed only to plumb the dark depths of the earth. ",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "When the world was sundered by the Well of Eternity's implosion, the earthen were deeply affected. Reeling with the pain of the earth itself, the earthen lost much of their identity and sealed themselves within the stone chambers where they were first created. Uldaman, Uldum, Ulduar... these were the names of the ancient Titan cities where the earthen first took shape and form. Buried deep beneath the world, the earthen rested in peace for nearly eight thousand years. ",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "Though it is unclear what awakened them, the earthen sealed within Uldaman eventually arose from their self-imposed slumber. These earthen found that they had changed significantly during their hibernation. Their rocky hides had softened and become smooth skin, and their powers over stone and earth had waned. They had become mortal creatures.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "Calling themselves dwarves, the last of the earthen left the halls of Uldaman and ventured out into the waking world. Still lulled by the safety and wonders of the deep places, they founded a vast kingdom under the highest mountain in the land. ",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "They named their land Khaz Modan, or \"Mountain of Khaz\", in honor of the Titan shaper, Khaz'goroth. Constructing an altar for their Titan father, the dwarves crafted a mighty forge within the heart of the mountain. Thus, the city that grew around the forge would be called Ironforge ever after.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "The dwarves, by nature fascinated with shaping gems and stone, set out to mine the surrounding mountains for riches and precious minerals. Content with their labors under the world, the dwarves remained isolated from the affairs of their surface-dwelling neighbors.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ironforge - the Awakening of the Dwarves",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 175736,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-631317"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "What was this?\r\n\r\nA bracer? \r\n\r\nIt seems quite small.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Leather Band",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 631317,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579243"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "But their dedication to their unknowable patterns is why they hate the fungarians. The very nature of fungarians disrupts things, and this drives the rutaani into a frenzy.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tending the Lands--Part 2: The Plan",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579243,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620325"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This set of tablets is old and weathered but seems like it has been well taken care of. However, only parts of them are legible.>\r\n\r\nPraise Akil'zon, whose covenant with our ruling family ensures our victory endures.\r\n\r\nPraise Jan'alai that our line of leaders through birth and death continues forever.\r\n\r\nPraise Halazzi for the clever Witherbark scribes who keep our records.\r\n\r\nPraise Nalorakk that these tablets, their archive, and our home that holds them never falls.\r\n\r\nAnd most of all praise ZUL'JIN who commissioned these tablets to renew our records and preserve our history that has been lost.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE SLOPES OF ZANDALAR\r\n\r\nCountless ages of our history have been lost either due to loss of elders keeping our oral traditions, or disasters and war.\r\n\r\nWhat is written here has been researched by Witherbark scholars and scribes commissioned by our warlord, ZUL'JIN.\r\n\r\nIN THE BEGINNING, the five (the Amani, the Witherbark, the Revantusk, the Shadowpine, and even the Vilebranch) tribes were one: THE AMANI--one family. And at the head was our patriarch MANZAJIN. He fought against the Zandalari, their greed, and their subjugation, to carve out borders of a new, free land.\r\n\r\nThe Amani continued for centuries in stability despite the Zandalari refusing to recognize the authority of the Amani tribe.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE MIGRATION\r\n\r\nThe names of MANZAJIN'S descendents have been lost, but what we do know is this: they pledged to rid the northeast of Kith'ix and the aqir and our bonds to the Zandalari.\r\n\r\nAs they traveled, they found their ability to call upon the loa weakened by the distance from their lands and the meddling of Kith'ix.\r\n\r\nEven so, their armies dispatched Kith'ix. The Amani cleansed the aqir from the land and created the vast Atal'Utek as a monument to their great battle but forbade entrance to its temple. \r\n\r\nWith this great victory began the AMANI EMPIRE OF ZUL'AMAN!",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE LOA OF ZUL'AMAN\r\n\r\nIt was in this time that the Amani became known to the loa of Zul'Aman and they to us. At first, we worshipped many, some worshipping still the loa of the Zandalari like Shadra and Hir'eek but, due to the distance, often not receiving their blessing. Others worshipped minor loa.\r\n\r\nBut soon from the line of Zul'jin came the first Amani leader with the title hash'ey, Kindo'jan. Kindo'jan received the blessing of the four most powerful loa of Zul'Aman--Akil'zon, Halazzi, Jan'alai, and Nalorakk, and thus also the minor loa in the region.\r\n\r\nHe was so beloved of Akil'zon that from then on, the loa became not only the Loa of VICTORY but also the Loa of the Amani tribe and its leaders.\r\n\r\nKindo'jan commissioned the temple city of Atal'Aman and the temples Akil'alor, Jan'alor, Halaz'alor, and Nal'alor.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE HASH'EY\r\n\r\nKindo'jan the hash'ey lived a long life spanning many generations. He established the order of the Loa Speakers and formalized the worshipful rituals we use still. Families began to group together near the temples of the loa that they worshipped most.\r\n\r\nThe Amani ruling family and others that worshipped Akil'zon settled in the temple city Atal'Aman and Amani'Zar.\r\n\r\nThe Witherbark settled in the region known as the Witherbark Bluffs.\r\n\r\nThe Shadowpine settled near Jan'alor and the islands around it, moving with the seasons.\r\n\r\nThe Revantusk settled near Nalorakk's Prowl.\r\n\r\nAnd the Vilebranch settled near Maisara, still clinging to the loa of the old lands.\r\n\r\nDespite living a long life, the hash'ey left no direct descendants, and encouraged his people to choose their next leader for their strength in mind, body, and spirit.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: ATAI'NATHA\r\n\r\nDespite his wish, perhaps due to their love of Kindo'jan, ATAI'NATHA, distant relative of Kindo'jan from a colony near Zandalar, assumed the throne. He was conceited and vain in his appearance. He wore his scarlet hair long and had his tusks capped with gold and gems, in the style of the Zandalari.\r\n\r\nHe worshipped the loa, but they had no love for him. Akil'zon liked not the look in his eye, Halazzi the deception in his voice, Nalorakk his strange smell, and Jan'alai the darkness in his heart.\r\n\r\nThey were right to not trust him. He had a claw of precious gems and gold to wear made for him, but in secret, he had Vilebranch crafters use old, dark magic to give it power.\r\n\r\nWith it, he ruthlessly expanded Zul'Aman's borders, but also would use his claw to kill anyone who dissented. In the end, he was poisoned by his own servants at the urging of the chieftains of the other Amani tribes. \r\n\r\nHis claw was destroyed and so ended his life and rule.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: REVANTUSK RISING\r\n\r\nThe death of Atai'natha left the Amani in disarray until NOROBU THE SCARRED, general of the Amani and leader of the Revantusk, stepped forward to be tested--and won. After days of feasting and deliberating, Norobu was made leader.\r\n\r\nNorobu created a council consisting of the chief of each tribe and bade them to meet at Amani'Zar. \r\n\r\nDevout of Nalorakk, he knew war would come, but in the time between, decreed that the Amani fortify themselves.\r\n\r\nHe fortified Atal'Aman with stone, built walls, and commissioned the Throne of Manzajin: a place where the council could meet but also engage in sport, feasting, and celebration.\r\n\r\nNorobu, who held no ill will toward Atai'natha after his death, adopted his children, who revered him and never sought the throne.\r\n\r\nNorobu ushered in a new tradition of only the worthy of spirit, mind, and body ruling Zul'Aman.",
},
{
["Page"] = 8,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: BEFORE THE SUNDERING\r\n\r\nTheir names are lost, but based on ancient carvings, after Norobu's death, the duty of chieftain shifted from tribe to tribe, and our tribes--the Revantusk and the Witherbark--reached out in trade to other troll nations, establishing settlements of their own.\r\n\r\nLong after we settled away from Zandalar, we found war again--this time against our most hated foe: the elves. Before what the gokinye call \"The Sundering,\" the Pale Queen's empire spread far to the east, encroaching on our lands. Despite our skirmishes with them and mutual hatred, the Zandalari kings and Azshara struck a bargain, ceding land to them to end hostilities.\r\n\r\nWe saw this not as \"shrewd diplomacy,\" but as weakness.\r\n\r\nWhen the earth cracked, we thought the raging sea would keep the elves away, but they returned. They sacked the sacred burial site of our hash'ey, the markets of Tor'Yunta, and with magic created a new city--Silvermoon.\r\n\r\nOur hatred began anew.",
},
{
["Page"] = 9,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THALASSIAN WAR\r\n\r\nThe destruction of Tor'Yunta and the loss of Atal'Kindo caused us a great distress and sparked wars over years without number.\r\n\r\nFinally, Chieftain Tan'dani, a cunning strategist of the Witherbark tribe, led our forces into battle, slowly gaining ground in guerilla attacks but also suffering heavy losses.\r\n\r\nIt was then the Zandalari, from over the waters, offered us aid. They would help us regain our territory with nothing in return but good will.\r\n\r\nTan'dari saw through their offer. She knew that with their help came the eventual vassalage of the Amani Empire.\r\n\r\nBut during a diplomatic journey to meet with the Zandalari ambassadors, she disappeared. The Zandalari, with their belief in castes and hereditary rule, put a young but fierce Amani of royal blood--able to trace his line to Manzajin--on the throne.\r\n\r\nThus began the rule of JINTHA.",
},
{
["Page"] = 10,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: BATTLE FOR ATAL'KINDO\r\n\r\nWith JINTHA, heir of the Amani, back on the throne, the Amani set to scour the elven city conjured from air and the well from our lands. A combined army of both humans and elves poised to attack on different flanks.\r\n\r\nThinking the humans easy prey, Jintha attacked the humans on his southern flank, but fell into a trap made by the humans and elves there.\r\n\r\nJintha perished in the flames produced by the human mages. Seeing this, the Zandalari abandoned the fight and the Amani were forced to retreat behind the current boundary of Zul'Aman.\r\n\r\nIt is unclear who took over from Jintha as ruler, but it seems as though the role passed from the tribe again.\r\n\r\nFinally, ZUL'JIN of the AMANI was tested and began a new age.",
},
{
["Page"] = 11,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE REIGN OF ZUL'JIN\r\n\r\nThe reign of WARLORD ZUL'JIN marked a new beginning for our people ushering in an era of pride in our culture and a return as a world power.\r\n\r\nZul'jin reunited the tribes of the Witherbark, Revantusk, Shadowpine, and Vilebranch as one Amani.\r\n\r\nHe fought valiantly against the elves, keeping them off balance and away from Zul'Aman, always looking for a way to rid them from our lands for good.\r\n\r\nAfter being captured and rescued by the Horde, he allied with them in return for restoring our homeland.\r\n\r\nBut the Horde abandoned the fight and Zul'jin's army was pushed back by the elves in Doomhammer's War.\r\n\r\nYayo'jin the Mystic prophesied Zul'jin would harness a power greater than anyone had ever known and that the time of a new hash'ey was near.\r\n\r\nKnowing now that he can trust no one but his Amani, his advisor, Malacrass, wise hexpriest of the Vilebranch, has promised to help him secure the power to reclaim what's ours.",
},
{
["Page"] = 12,
["Text"] = "<It is clear that the etching on the top of the tablet has been ground down, and a sorrowful carving of a funeral procession has been carved on top of it. Based on the letters you can still discern underneath, you can tell this tablet was supposed to be on the continuation of Zul'jin's reign--not his death.>\r\n\r\nTHE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE DEATH OF ZUL'JIN\r\n\r\nOn the eve of obtaining the power to conquer the elves and return our lands, we were beset by an army of gokinye who invaded our temple city of Atal'Aman.\r\n\r\nOur warlord has died. Malacrass's body has not been recovered, and his only heir, Man'ye, the Aspect of Akil'zon, has died as well.\r\n\r\nWe know not what transpired within Atal'Aman. All that fought there are dead. Even the loa are silent in our defeat either in sorrow, anger, or shame.\r\n\r\nYoung ZUL'JARRA, Man'ye's daughter, already shows great promise. ZARAMA, her mother, will reign until she can be tested.\r\n\r\nLong live ZUL'JARRA long live ZARAMA.",
},
{
["Page"] = 13,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: \r\n\r\n<Much of the top of this tablet's text has been obliterated and recarved in a threatening motif of warriors with their tusks bared and their eyes wide.\r\n\r\nHowever, you can make out two chieftain entries. You believe the names are likely KAZRA'JIN and DAAKARA. You can also make out something referencing the name Zul.>\r\n\r\nDuring the turmoil that was beget by Zul'jin's death, the tribe fractured, some wanting to claim the power Zul'jin sought, others later to conquer abroad with the help of the Zandalari. They led many, but had selfish aims.\r\n\r\nThey were laid low by fate. Let no one mourn them! And let no one cross our borders under pain of death!",
},
},
},
