["GameObject-579201"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The haranir are not people who fear, but we often tie ourselves to tradition. We came to this land to keep it safe. We will find the source of its light and the reason for its absence, even if tradition must be cast aside.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Awe'ohna's Path--Part 1: Questions",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579201,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-668593"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Here lies a soul beyond comparison. I dreamt of our life together. Now you may rest while I must dream new dreams.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Funerary Inscription",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 668593,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613823"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This ancient runestone has a carving of several haranir standing on a forested mountain. They look below at another group of haranir following a ball that radiates wave-like energy. The ball is taking them deep underground to a cave filled with many roots.\r\n\r\nThis carving appears to depict a split within the Haranir society, leading to one group staying on the surface, while the other takes the journey to Harandar.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ancient Runestone",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613823,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620324"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Loyalty! Grit!\r\n\r\nThose that beseech the bear loa Nalorakk must have both!\r\n\r\nNalorakk--when the mountain wakes, shakes off his slumber, his steps, like war drums, portend death without number.\r\n\r\nHe is called by many names:\r\n\r\nThe Dreamer\r\n\r\nThe Mountain\r\n\r\nIronjaw\r\n\r\nStonehide\r\n\r\nThe Unyielding One\r\n\r\nThe Revantusk call upon Nalorakk to increase their strength in battle, but also to protect and fortify their dens. As he endures in battle, he makes strong the walls of our settlements and protects our fields and crops. He is celebrated with the harvest; the food that gives our warriors strength comes from the earth--his domain. But also the harsh winter through which the god slumbers. The hearth, our home, our soldiers, harvest--only are made safe and endure through Nalorakk the loa of WAR!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Nalorakk",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620324,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-544004"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Cursed Gurubashi bind us\r\nFang of Shadra pry the bars\r\nBlood of Hir'eek mark the way\r\nBy their corpses we be freed",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Embossed Tablet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 544004,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-553848"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Staff of Disintegration\r\n\r\nSome foes are only stopped when they are erased from existence. Such was Met'imua, an Amani who fought during the Troll Wars. He could regenerate so quickly that no blade, arrow, or spell could fell him. The Staff of Disintegration was crafted to overcharge arcane power, and used to eliminate every trace of Met'imua and his home.\r\n\r\nSo horrific was the carnage that both the staff and its creator were locked away, until it was taken by Grand Astromancer Capernian to Tempest Keep. The staff now rests in the light of the Sunwell, in hopes of cleansing its tragic past.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Staff of Disintegration",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 553848,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-290682"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "HERE LIE -\r\nKing Rahu'ai and his trusted advisors, Atu and M'bara. Long did he rule. Painful was his fall.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Placard",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 290682,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-290694"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "HERE LIES -\r\nZanazal the Wise, born to rule, beset by enemies, and resilient enough to endure a civil war that few others did. Though he never saw the others as his equal, he nevertheless saw the value in keeping his enemies close.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Placard",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 290694,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-60977"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Zaren,\r\n\r\nYour first objective is to take and hold the Cathedral Quarter of Gilneas City. From there I want you to work with Lord Crowley's worgen to push forward into enemy territory. Take out their near outposts and cut their lines of communication.\r\n\r\nKing Wrynn has assured me that a full armada of warships is en route and should be arriving any day. Once the rest of the fleet is here, we will launch an all out assault on Forsaken Forward Command and beat those worthless maggots back into Silverpine Forest\r\n\r\nOnce Gilneas is securely in Alliance control, we will begin preparations for retaking Lordaeron.\r\n\r\nFor the glory of the Alliance!\r\n\r\n-High Commander Halford Wyrmbane\r\n\r\nP.S. We will launch a signal flare when we are ready to attack Forsaken Forward Command. Keep your soldiers on high alert.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Orders from High Command",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 60977,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-613818"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "It was in the years that followed the rise of the ancient winged beasts that even we dared not hunt that the stone giants scoured our lands.\r\n\r\nWe knew of the poison in their ways and so we hid from their watching eyes. While some saw glory in tales of the stone armies banishing the ancient chaos that had covered the old world, we stayed away.\r\n\r\nWe had no interest in their great halls, or strange rituals. Our people listened to the song that came from within, not to the monotone staccato of their ordered march.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tarnished Mural",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613818,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-587287"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "These remains look ready to crumble to dust at the slightest touch. Scratch marks mar the stone all over the room.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ancient Troll Skeleton",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 587287,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579202"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Our traditions forbid entering Aln'hara's Cradle. Even the beasts of this land do not fly there--only the roots. But I cannot let our land die for tradition.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Awe'ohna's Path--Part 2: Answers",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579202,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-290697"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "HERE LIES -\r\nDazar, the First King. He who raised us beyond the curse of blood. He who defied the Dark One. He who built an empire.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Placard",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 290697,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620327"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Imagination! Child-like Wonder!\r\n\r\nThose protected by Filo must have both.\r\n\r\nBeware those would  harm children lest you stoke the ire of Filo and his brethren! Learn of Filo's dark side and nowhere but DEATH can you hide.\r\n\r\nFilo is called by many names:\r\n\r\nFirst Friend\r\n\r\nUncle Filo\r\n\r\nThe Guardian\r\n\r\n\r\nChildren have no need to worship, no need to call him. All Amani children earn his protection. The youngest child of every village is his speaker. Filo says nothing, but all understand.\r\n\r\nOther loa fear Filo's power. Nothing can kill him, and his rage is insatiable. But he is focused. Placid enough to eat from a child's hand but ruthless enough to kill the most powerful warrior if it suits him.\r\n\r\nFilo protects children beyond death. If a child dies before its mother or father, Filo and his attendants gather and wait with the child until their parents come to guide them.\r\n\r\nTo reach Filo, come to him and play. Only a child or the purest of heart hold him in sway.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Filo",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620327,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620321"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Patience! Cleverness!\r\n\r\nThose who follow Halazzi have both.\r\n\r\nHalazzi--the silver lynx that stalks the night, waiting hides from all sight.\r\n\r\nHe is called by many names!\r\n\r\nLong Ear\r\n\r\nThe Silver Shadow\r\n\r\nThe Schemer\r\n\r\nThe Night Hunter\r\n\r\nThe Witherbark call upon Halazzi to hide them from their prey, to help them outwit their enemies, to protect them in the night, and to increase their grace in dance and in combat. He brings the mist and rain keeping plants and animals of the forest fit for the hunt. His ears and eyes like the moon pierce the veil revealing lies, mysteries, motivations and the unseen. Praise the playful lynx loa of games, of the moon, of shadow, of the forest, and the HUNT!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Halazzi",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620321,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613847"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<A haphazard collection of notes, diagrams, and letters documenting changes in the Dead Scar. Some writings are several years old, while others are more recent.>\r\n\r\nIt has been two months since my field experiment. The longer I sit with the knowledge that this taint is irreversible, the less I can bear it.\r\n\r\nPerhaps I made a mistake. The magistrix agreed with my research, but perhaps she was also mistaken.\r\n\r\nI have to keep looking.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "<Written on the back of a lengthy research log.>\r\n\r\nToday marks the end of a full year of testing. I have taken so many soil samples, stained more crates than I care to document, and yet I have nothing to show.\r\n\r\nSo many cleansing spells, draughts, runes. But still nothing will grow in that soil. No matter how carefully I tend to the seeds, they wither to ash within hours.\r\n\r\nIt cannot be hopeless. I refuse to let it be hopeless.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "<Scribbled at the bottom of a report dated years later:>\r\n\r\nI am so tired.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "<A map of Quel'Thalas with a few frantically scribbled circles near the top of the Dead Scar.>\r\n\r\nPeacebloom shoots!",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "<Several diagrams of the Sunwell, accompanied by pages upon pages of complex magical equations.>\r\n\r\nThe growth started in the very north, but it has begun trickling southward over the past months.\r\n\r\nI found a few patches of grass as far down as the East Sanctum yesterday.\r\n\r\nGRASS!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Mirveda's Notes",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613847,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613827"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "We left the surface to follow the call, to seek the song from the depths, the voice we did not yet know.\r\n\r\nThere were concerns about what those who decided to stay on the surface would do in our absence.\r\n\r\nWe knew what lurked in the places of myth. We were venturing into forbidden parts of the ancient world.\r\n\r\nWill it still be our concern if or when their children wake up the dark sleeping beneath them? Is it still our world to save when they engulf it with the flames of their curiosity?\r\n\r\nHope is to believe they listened to the warnings and pass them down to the generations to come.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Derelict Mural",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613827,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-631316"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The arm reaches out.\r\n\r\nThere was something important here long ago.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Troll Bones",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 631316,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
